# Phase 2b: replication at the K7-tuned LRs (pre-registered in experiments/checks/PREDICTIONS.md,
# "Replication protocol"). NOT a campaign file: experiments/checks/k7_lr_sweep.py --write-campaign
# fills {LR_E10} / {LR_E1} and resolves the #IF_ lines into phase2b-replication.campaign.
# Full 200M-token runs (the registered max_tokens). Estimated wall time per run, from the v0.3.0
# runs incl. compile and evals: E10 ~23 min (assumed = E0), E1 ~39 min, E11 ~39 min (assumed = E1),
# E9 ~33 min, E0 ~23 min,
# E2 ~80 min; plus 60 s gaps.
E10 --seed 0 --lr {LR_E10}
E10 --seed 1 --lr {LR_E10}
E10 --seed 2 --lr {LR_E10}
E1  --seed 0 --lr {LR_E1}
E1  --seed 1 --lr {LR_E1}
E1  --seed 2 --lr {LR_E1}
# E11 (negative-eigenvalue GDN on the E1 stack): compared with E1's 3-seed mean at the same LR
# (its own registry prediction; criterion max(1%, 2x pooled seed std)).
E11 --seed 0 --lr {LR_E1}
E11 --seed 1 --lr {LR_E1}
E11 --seed 2 --lr {LR_E1}
# E9: the unlooped control for E2, at E1's tuned LR (its committed prediction assumed 3e-3).
E9  --seed 0 --lr {LR_E1}
# Implementation parity: our dense E0 at the control's tuned LR (skipped when that is 3e-3,
# because the v0.3.0 E0 seed-0 run is already at 3e-3).
#IF_E10_NOT_3e-3 E0  --seed 0 --lr {LR_E10}
# E2 at the same LR as E9, so the loop-vs-no-loop comparison is at one LR (skipped when 3e-3).
#IF_E1_NOT_3e-3 E2  --seed 0 --lr {LR_E1}
